r}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3591843208","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2922#issuecomment-3591843208","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2922","id":3591843208,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887WFy2I","user":{"login":"liorsl","id":29403941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NDAzOTQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29403941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl","html_url":"https://github.com/liorsl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-29T18:08:58Z","updated_at":"2025-11-29T18:10:14Z","body":"Just my 2 cents here, but unless using OIDC the owner of the device doesn't have any control over the user that the device is assigned to in the first place. I understand Headscale is an OSS project but I just want to mention not having this command anymore will make my (and I am sure other users as well) experience just a lot harder. I have personally used the aforementioned move command quite a lot. \r\nOf course, I appreciate the work you guys do for the community, as a developer I understand the time spent here. I don't want to sound entitled but just to voice my own personal opinion","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3591843208/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"liorsl","id":29403941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NDAzOTQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29403941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl","html_url":"https://github.com/liorsl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/liorsl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3596348461","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2922#issuecomment-3596348461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2922","id":3596348461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887WW-wt","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-01T12:38:18Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T12:38:18Z","body":"> One of the problems associated with this would be similar to the email takeover on an OIDC platform.\r\n\r\nIt might have been a mistake to include this part, the point of this statement isnt to imply that this is being removed because of OIDC and such, it is just to highlight a similar attack surface. \r\n\r\nWe are removing it because of OIDC or the similar, but because it is a feature that does not align with the security model that Tailscale has, and particularly as a reimplementation, it is so easy to introduce security issues, and this is a step in the direction of minimising the possibility to do that.\r\n\r\nInstead of moving a device, the correct path is to just reauthenticate it, which is relatively trivial. ","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3596348461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/